/-!
# Native triality short-root centralizers

For binary parameters q > 2, the marked highest short root has its full
centralizer in the central parabolic and a designated positive Sylow
intersection. The fixed-tree proof also identifies the unique vertex fixed
by that full centralizer. Its characteristic elementary long-root plane
has a faithful PSL₂(q) action and a single orbit on nonzero vectors. See
the imported modules for Aschbacher–Smith F.4.27(4)(ii), the native premise
of F.4.40, and the action used in F.4.42.
-/
